{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reference value is determined as zero, since there is no sure outcome (i.e., no outcome with 100% probability) in either lottery. The differences between each outcome and the reference value (zero) are simply the outcomes themselves: for Lottery A, 6000 (25%) and 0 (75%); for Lottery B, 4000 (25%), 2000 (25%), and 0 (50%). The mean difference for each lottery is the expected value: Lottery A: 0.25 × 6000 = 1500; Lottery B: 0.25 × 4000 + 0.25 × 2000 = 1000 + 500 = 1500. Both lotteries have the same mean difference (1500). Thus, the decision reason would be indifferent between A and B.",
